artist_wiki": "https://cs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Různí_interpreti"}}, {"id": 646, "num": "0636", "genre": "New Orleans Brass Band", "rec": "Various - The Music of New Orleans, Vol. 3 - Music of the Dance Halls (1951-1954)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "New Orleans Brass Band", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Various+-+The+Music+of+New+Orleans%2C+Vol.+3+-+Music+of+the+Dance+Halls", "x": 2270, "y": 344, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Sensation Of The Day", "year": 1961, "artist_name": "Nemours Jean-Baptiste"}}, {"id": 647, "num": "0637", "genre": "New Orleans Brass Band", "rec": "Various - Music From the South - Volume 1 - Country Brass Bands (1955)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "New Orleans Brass Band", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Various+-+Music+From+the+South+-+Volume+1+-+Country+Brass+Bands", "x": 2530, "y": 344, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Sermon!", "year": 1959, "artist_name": "Jimmy Smith", "country": "US"}}, {"id": 648, "num": "0638", "genre": "New Orleans Brass Band", "rec": "Olympia Brass Band - Here Come da Great Olympia Band (1974)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "New Orleans Brass Band", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Olympia+Brass+Band+-+Here+Come+da+Great+Olympia+Band", "x": 2790, "y": 344, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Shape of Jazz to Come", "year": 1959, "artist_name": "Ornette Coleman", "country": "US", "cover_url": "https://ia801308.us.archive.org/19/items/mbid-c4a1b794-7bb5-411a-a876-7af045cf6f22/mbid-c4a1b794-7bb5-411a-a876-7af045cf6f22-12407949899.jpg", "rateyourmusic_url": "https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/ornette-coleman/the-shape-of-jazz-to-come-4", "desc_album": "Ornette Coleman's Atlantic debut, The Shape of Jazz to Come, was a watershed event in the genesis of avant-garde jazz, profoundly steering its future course and throwing down a gauntlet that some still haven't come to grips with. The record shattered traditional concepts of harmony in jazz, getting rid of not only the piano player but the whole idea of concretely outlined chord changes. The pieces here follow almost no predetermined harmonic structure, which allows Coleman and partner Don Cherry an unprecedented freedom to take the melodies of their solo lines wherever they felt like going in ", "desc_artist": "Ornette Coleman (March 9, 1930 - June 11, 2015) was an American jazz saxophonist, violinist, trumpeter, and composer. He was one of the founders and major innovators of the 1960s free jazz movement and one of the most notable figures in jazz history.\n\nColeman was born in 1930 in Fort Worth, Texas where he participated in his high school band until being dismissed for improvising during \"The Washin", "aoty_user_score": 82}}, {"id": 650, "num": "0640", "genre": "Dixieland", "rec": "Original Dixieland Jazz Band - The First Jazz Recordings (1917-1921)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "Dixieland", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Original+Dixieland+Jazz+Band+-+The+First+Jazz+Recordings", "x": 3050, "y": 344, "rel_out": ["0641", "0642", "0643", "0644", "0645", "0646", "0647", "0648", "0649", "0650"], "alb": {"album_name": "The Swan Lake", "year": 2015, "artist_name": "The USSR State Symphony Orchestra & Evgeni Svetlanov"}}, {"id": 651, "num": "0641", "genre": "Dixieland", "rec": "Freddie Keppard - The Complete Set (1923-1926)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "Dixieland", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Freddie+Keppard+-+The+Complete+Set", "x": 3310, "y": 344, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Texas-Czech, Bohemian-Moravian Bands: Historic Recordings 1929-1959", "year": 1993, "artist_name": "Various Artists", "artist_mb": "https://musicbrainz.org/artist/89ad4ac3-39f7-470e-963a-56509c546377", "artist_wiki": "https://cs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Různí_interpreti"}}, {"id": 652, "num": "0642", "genre": "Dixieland", "rec": "King Oliver - The Chronogical Classics (1923-1926)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "Dixieland", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=King+Oliver+-+The+Chronogical+Classics", "x": 2010, "y": 474, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Transfiguration of Blind Joe Death", "year": 1965, "artist_name": "John Fahey", "country": "US", "cover_url": "https://dn721608.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-7c121291-82aa-4031-8d26-c5f7a18f0c72/mbid-7c121291-82aa-4031-8d26-c5f7a18f0c72-41742393957.jpg", "desc_album": "A disgusting, degenerate, insipid young folklorist from the Croat & Isaiah Nettles Foundation for Ethnological Research meandered mesmerically midst marble mansions in Mattapan, Massachusetts. It was an unsavory, vapid day in the summer of 2010 as the jejune air from Back Bay transubstantiated itself autologically and gradually into an ozone-like atmosphere. Knocking on a random door, haphazardly, the tasteless young man pondered the Hebraic inscription on the marble-tiled foot-brush, soporifically: \"I wonder what the hell that means,\" he said to himself reflexively. The foot-brush backed itse", "desc_artist": "John Aloysius Fahey (February 28, 1939 – February 22, 2001) was an American fingerstyle guitarist and composer who played the steel-string acoustic guitar as a solo instrument. His style has been greatly influential and has been described as the foundation of American Primitive Guitar, a term borrowed from painting and referring mainly to the self-taught nature of the music and its minimalist styl"}}, {"id": 653, "num": "0643", "genre": "Dixieland", "rec": "Louis Armstrong - The Best of Louis Armstrong - The Hot Five and Hot Seven Recordings (1925-1929)", "cat": "JAZZ", "fam": "Dixieland", "yt": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Louis+Armstrong+-+The+Best+of+Louis+Armstrong+-+The+Hot+Five+and+Hot+Seven+Recordings", "x": 2270, "y": 474, "rel_out": [], "alb": {"album_name": "The Voice of Frank Sinatra", "year": 1946, "artist_name": "Frank Sinatra", "country": "US"}}, {"id": 654, "num": "0644", "genre": "Dixieland", "rec": "Jelly Roll Morton - Birth of the Hot 